traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 44% in the 2020 crash, 42% in the 2022 bear market and 67% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $36.24 (margin of safety -273%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 30%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $26.89 to $48.86 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: EV/EBITDA 18.9 vs 13.3 and P/FCF 38.6 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 114% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 2.6% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 20 covering analysts target $175 on average, 29% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 8% falls short of the cost of capital of 9.4%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.75).","It runs a 33% gross margin and converts 9% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.78x.","ROE of 25% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.9x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.2% of revenue on R&D and 0.6% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.8x net debt to EBITDA ($379.0M of cash against $9.3B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 7.1x.","The current ratio of 0.93 means short-term liabilities exceed current assets.","Goodwill makes up 44% of assets, a soft asset exposed to impairment."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -2.3% over 3 years, 1.1% over 5 years and 9.1% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 70%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 0.8% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are expanding (+1.1% trend).","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 1.07 (orders outpacing sales), a backlog worth 96% of annual revenue and deferred revenue up 14%.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (1.8% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.2%), and institutions hold 92%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (10 sales, net $18.1M sold).","It returns 8.5% a year to shareholders (7.3% in buybacks and 1.2% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.8% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 38 consecutive years, raising it 4.3% a year over the last five."],"people":["CEO pay is $4.0M."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":41,"head":"Avoid: priced 273% above its fair value of $36.24.","pros":["20 analysts' mean target $175 (+29%)","12-1 month momentum +31%","Operating margin expanding 1.1%/yr","Returns 8.5% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Trades 273% above fair value of $36.24","ROIC 8.4% vs WACC 9.4%","EV/EBITDA 18.9x vs sector 13.3x","P/FCF 38.6x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":["Priced 273% above its fair value of $36.24"],"need":[],"buy_below":30.8,"vc":{"base":36.24,"base_src":"dcf","bear":26.89,"bull":48.86,"alt_median":28.48,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.389,"dispersion":0.297,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"JCI","date":"2026-11-06"}